kernelbase: GetIntegratedDisplaySize() exists, as the stub upstream Wine has.

Upstream Wine c68ed23672 (Paul Gofman, 2025-11-20, "kernelbase: Add stub for
GetIntegratedDisplaySize()"), which the CrossOver 26.3 tree does not carry: its kernelbase.spec still
has the entry commented out. With no export at all the loader binds a program's import to the
"unimplemented function" thunk, and calling it raises.

Forza Horizon 6 imports the function from api-ms-win-core-sysinfo-l1-2-3 and calls it once its
window is up, to learn whether it runs on a handheld. On x64-crossover26.3-r17 with D3DMetal 4.0b2
(M4, macOS 27.0, 2026-10-05) the game opened its 1920x1080 window, compiled pipelines and then
stopped with "Call from 00006FFFFFF9EC2A to unimplemented function
api-ms-win-core-sysinfo-l1-2-3.dll.GetIntegratedDisplaySize, aborting" and its own crash dialog.
The game returns the HRESULT to its caller, so a failure is an answer it accepts.

--- a/dlls/kernelbase/kernelbase.spec
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/kernelbase.spec
@@ -569,7 +569,7 @@
 @ stdcall GetGeoInfoEx(ptr long ptr long)
 @ stdcall GetHandleInformation(long ptr)
 # @ stub GetHivePath
-# @ stub GetIntegratedDisplaySize
+@ stdcall GetIntegratedDisplaySize(ptr)
 # @ stub GetIsEdpEnabled
 @ stdcall GetKernelObjectSecurity(long long ptr long ptr)
 @ stdcall GetLargePageMinimum()
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/main.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/main.c
@@ -635,3 +635,9 @@ HRESULT WINAPI GetAcceptLanguagesW(WCHAR *langbuf, DWORD *buflen)
     *buflen = 0;
     return E_NOT_SUFFICIENT_BUFFER;
 }
+
+HRESULT WINAPI GetIntegratedDisplaySize( double *sz_inches )
+{
+    FIXME( "%p stub.\n", sz_inches );
+    return E_NOTIMPL;
+}
